\ choose{ resolves during the parse, before the AOT compiler sees the
\ instruction stream, so only the selected branch reaches the binary. All three
\ branches define `tag`; if the unselected branches were compiled the build
\ would fail with a duplicate const definition. It builds and prints the linux
\ value, proving the macos and _ branches are absent.
linux: choose{
  linux: [
    tag: ( -- n ) [ 1 ] ;
  ]
  macos: [
    tag: ( -- n ) [ 2 ] ;
  ]
  _ [
    tag: ( -- n ) [ 9 ] ;
  ]
}
tag .
